# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings. A CRLF docker-entrypoint.sh fails inside
# the Alpine container with a baffling "no such file or directory" - the kernel
# reads the shebang as "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist. Windows checkouts with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite it on clone.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Prisma emits migration SQL with LF; keep it byte-identical across platforms so
# the checksum Prisma records for an applied migration stays stable.
*.sql text eol=lf
